.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]SyntaxError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if an invalid unit was passed to the method.
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] on which the method is being called
can\(cqt be resolved to a single value and type.
This might occur if the value is calculated from a variable when the
value of that variable can\(cqt be known in the context.
.IP \(bu 2
The value can\(cqt be converted to the new unit because it\(cqs not of
the same category.
For example, you can\(cqt convert meters to seconds.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
